@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "If your licences come from a partner";
}

<h1>If your licences come from a partner</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Your Microsoft licences are sold to you by a Cloud Solution Provider. Microsoft does not give
    you &mdash; or us &mdash; access to what your partner charges you. That is a restriction of the
    channel, not a permission anyone can grant.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Two ways forward</h2>
<ol>
    <li>
        <strong>Enter your prices.</strong> Under <em>Prices</em>, type the per-seat price from
        your partner's invoice. All cost views will use it and show an
        <em>entered by you</em> badge.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Invite your partner.</strong> Send them the invite from
        <em>Settings &rarr; Partner</em>. If they join MLCP and choose to share pricing with you,
        prices and renewal settings appear automatically.
    </li>
</ol>

<p class="text-muted">
    Everything else &mdash; licences, who has what, usage, renewal dates, waste detection &mdash;
    works without either step.
</p>

<a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="Index">Back to connection status</a>
